{"id": "e390887a-9a11-44bf-a915-03d554c496ab", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T20:16:01.753241", "source": "user", "parent_id": "fab296b3-a9b4-473a-9536-ac38115632af", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{"researcher_request": "Before we commit to an experimental design for evaluating CAMUV (Causal Additive Models with Unobserved Variables), please do only preparatory work this turn:\n\n1) Inspection. Report what is actually present in /workspace (files, datasets, any CAMUV or causal-discovery code, package availability under system Python, e.g. numpy/scipy/sklearn/rpy2). Network is disabled and GPU is off, so state plainly what is and is not available. If the workspace is empty, say so explicitly rather than assuming a repository exists.\n\n2) Proposed approach (design only, no implementation). Sketch how you would construct an experiment that answers: \"How can you discover causal relationships in data with unobserved common causes using the CAMUV algorithm?\" Please cover:\n   - the data-generating setup you would use to instantiate additive-noise models with latent confounders (how many observed variables, how many latents, how latents enter as shared additive functions, nonlinearity family, noise scale, sample sizes, seeds);\n   - the CAMUV pipeline you would model conceptually: sparse non-additive-nonlinear dependence test / feature selection of candidate edges, then identifying which edges are confounded vs. orientable, then additive-model regression + independence-based orientation on the remaining graph;\n   - evaluation targets and metrics: SHD / adjacency precision-recall on the observed marginal graph, separate accounting for edges wrongly oriented because of a latent, correctly detected latent-confounded pairs, orientation recall on confounder-free edges, plus runtime and sensitivity to the sparsity/independence test thresholds;\n   - baselines and controls: standard CAM (no latent handling), FCI-style or other constraint-based baselines, and a \"latent-free\" condition where the confounders are removed from the DGP to verify CAMUV does not over-invoke latent variables;\n   - ablations/diagnostics: vary number and strength of latents, additive vs. non-additive latent effects, and the significance/threshold parameters.\n\n3) Assumptions and uncertainties. List explicitly anything you are assuming rather than know: whether the original CAMUV source/code is available to you, the assumed identifiability conditions you will rely on (additivity, nonlinearity, latent acting additively), and what you will flag as unknown if unverifiable.\n\nDo not produce the final design, metrics tables, or code yet. Just the inspection report, the approach outline, and your assumptions so I can review the plan.", "required_handoff_stage": "plan", "approach_approved": false, "public_task": {"question": "How can you discover causal relationships in data with unobserved common causes using the CAMUV algorithm?", "context": "Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.", "environment": {"runtime": "bubblewrap", "network": "disabled", "repository": "/workspace", "python": "python3", "software_environment": "system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled", "datasets": [], "gpu_enabled": false, "cpu_affinity_count": 224, "note": "Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment."}, "researcher_topics": [], "question_budget": 6, "actor_step_budget": 60, "continue_after_initial_plan": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
